  instead of "...across the tropics") — fixed there 2026-08-25. Confirmed via search: based on 5M+
  household interviews across 85 tropical countries, finds 1.2 billion people (30%) highly
  dependent on nature for direct subsistence use. This is survey-based, single-time-point, and
  tropics-only (not global, not a multi-decade trend, not remote-sensing/InVEST-based) — supports
  the "declining provision falls disproportionately on populations with limited adaptive capacity"
  claim it's actually cited for, but does not compete with or resemble our paper's own analysis in
  method or scope. No further correction needed beyond the reference-list title fix.
