TY  - JOUR
AU  - Kim, H.
AU  - et al.
PY  - 2024
TI  - Global trends and scenarios for terrestrial biodiversity and ecosystem services from 1900 to 2050
JO  - Science
DO  - 10.1126/science.adn3441
UR  - https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/science.adn3441
N1  - REAL, CLOSE COMPETITOR — needs explicit citation and distinction, not silence. IPBES-affiliated
  multi-model ensemble: harmonized land-use/climate RECONSTRUCTIONS for 1900-2015 (i.e., modeled
  hindcasting, not direct observational/remote-sensing measurement) plus three future scenarios to
  2050. Covers multiple aggregated service classes (provisioning vs. regulating) globally. Key
  differences from our paper, all worth stating explicitly in the Introduction/lit-review pass: (1)
  historical portion is model-reconstructed, not built from direct 1992/2020 satellite-observed
  land cover + process-based biophysical modeling at 300m; (2) aggregated service-class trends, not
  spatially explicit hotspot identification at grid-cell resolution; (3) no downstream/travel-based
  beneficiary exposure analysis; (4) no land-cover-conversion attribution test. The novelty claim
  should be narrowed to name what specifically is new relative to this paper (resolution, realized
  vs. reconstructed data, hotspot/exposure/attribution framing), not asserted as if no comparable
  global multi-decade study exists at all.
ER  -

